questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Java microservice on OpenJDK 17 crashes with `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Metaspace` after running for several days. The service executes user-defined dynamic rules compiled at runtime using the following Spring bean component:

java
@Service
public class DynamicRuleEngine {
    public void executeRule(String ruleScript, Map<String, Object> context) {
        GroovyClassLoader classLoader = new GroovyClassLoader();
        Class<?> clazz = classLoader.parseClass(ruleScript);
        Rule rule = (Rule) clazz.getDeclaredConstructor().newInstance();
        rule.run(context);
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where a Spring Boot state manager periodically refreshes dynamic configuration properties consumed by multiple worker threads. Under load, worker threads occasionally read stale parameters or throw `NullPointerException`s immediately following a refresh, despite the setup attempting non-blocking updates:

java
@Component
public class DynamicConfigHolder {
    private Map<String, String> configMap = new HashMap<>();

    public void updateConfig(Map<String, String> newSettings) {
        Map<String, String> tempMap = new HashMap<>(newSettings);
        this.configMap = tempMap;
    }

    public String getConfig(String key) {
        return this.configMap.get(key);
    }
}
